{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","cve_id":"CVE-2026-109869","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","summary":"undici vulnerable to Denial of Service via unhandled error on excessive content-encodings","description":"### Impact\n\nundici's `fetch()` crashes the Node.js process when a malicious server returns a response with more than five content codings and closes the connection before sending the body. undici rejects such responses (a content-encoding limit), but it created the internal response stream before that check and returned without attaching an error listener or aborting the request. The early close then surfaces a content-length mismatch on that orphaned internal stream, which Node.js treats as an unhandled `error` and terminates the process. A remote, unauthenticated server can trigger this with a single response, even when the application correctly catches the `fetch()` rejection. undici 6.x, 7.x, and 8.x are affected.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `6.29.1`, `7.30.1`, or `8.12.2`. undici now validates the content-encoding chain before creating the internal body stream and aborts the response when the limit is exceeded, so no error can surface on an orphaned stream.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/security-advisories/GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","source_code_location":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-109869","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109869","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/07ded4941b1e72afec862958c3b8ddf468f3b429","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/1325a87dfb3492f8e87e6b0a84b3bda4e82e3436","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b5084c7dc239172d75c336b1cd51ddac023938a5","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v6.29.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.30.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.12.2","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xjj6-f33q-929c"],"published_at":"2026-10-23T22:14:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T22:14:32Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-23T22:14:31Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-15T19:17:21Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 6.23.0, < 6.29.1","first_patched_version":"6.29.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 7.18.0, < 7.30.1","first_patched_version":"7.30.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 8.0.0, < 8.12.2","first_patched_version":"8.12.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-248","name":"Uncaught Exception"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-459","name":"Incomplete Cleanup"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"hanityx","id":37394823,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3Mzk0ODIz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37394823?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx","html_url":"https://github.com/hanityx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hanityx/events{/